From: Fractal Microsystems <bsp@fractalmicro.org>
Subject: [PATCH] audio: keep ALSA overlap expressed in frames

The rounded-up period count was used as a frame count, reducing the
requested 20 ms scheduling margin to a handful of frames. Multiply by
period_size to retain that margin between streamed PCM chunks.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/src/audio/alsa.c
+++ b/src/audio/alsa.c
@@ -824,7 +824,7 @@ static int alsa_drain_overlap(AudioID * id, AudioTrack track)
 	if (2*period_size >= min)
 		min2 = 2*period_size;
 	else
-		min2 = (min + period_size - 1) / period_size;
+		min2 = ((min + period_size - 1) / period_size) * period_size;

 	/* Usually the buffer size will be far enough */
 	if (alsa_id->alsa_buffer_size >= min2)
